    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vŏcontii</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in</i> Gallia Narbonensis, <i>between
				the rivers Isara and</i>
			
			
			<i>Druentius</i>, now <i>Vaison</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Caes.
				B. G. 1, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 5, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4,
				5, § 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21,
				31, 9</span></i>; Planc. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 32, 2</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vŏ-contĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Vocontii</i>, <i>Vocontian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 467</span></i>
			.</div>
